# Normalize line endings for all text files: store as LF in the
# repository, check out using each platform's native convention (CRLF on
# Windows, LF on Linux/macOS). Without this file, git had no explicit,
# repo-scoped policy -- the Windows checkout only got consistent CRLF
# checkout/LF-storage behavior from this machine's Git for Windows
# installer default (system-level core.autocrlf=true, outside this
# repo's control), and a clone or bridge without that default sees
# whatever bytes happen to be on disk. This file makes the policy
# explicit and reproducible regardless of any one machine's git config.
* text=auto

# Explicitly binary -- never subject to line-ending or diff normalization.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
